 "titulo": {
  "estudio": "Dice que viene, dice que venga",
  "alumno": "She says he's coming, she says he should come"
 },
 "intro": "Verbs with two meanings. The mood after que tells you which one is meant.",
 "palabras": [
  {
   "palabra": "decir que",
   "significado": "to say that; to tell (someone) to",
   "pron": "de-THIR ke",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "With the indicative it reports a fact: «dice que viene». With the subjunctive it gives an order: «dice que venga».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "sentir que",
   "significado": "to sense that; to be sorry that",
   "pron": "sen-TIR ke",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Indicative: you sense it, «siento que hay un problema». Subjunctive: you regret it, «siento que haya un problema».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "insistir en que",
   "significado": "to maintain that; to demand that",
   "pron": "in-sis-TIR en ke",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "With the indicative it defends a fact; with the subjunctive it demands something: «insiste en que vayamos».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "recordar que",
   "significado": "to remind that; to remind to",
   "pron": "rre-kor-DAR ke",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "With the indicative you recall a fact; with the subjunctive you ask for something: «te recuerdo que llames».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "comprender que",
   "significado": "to realise that; to find it natural that",
   "pron": "kom-pren-DER ke",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Indicative: you see it, «comprendo que estás cansado». Subjunctive: you find it logical, «comprendo que estés cansado».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "el hecho de que",
   "significado": "the fact that",
   "pron": "el E-cho de ke",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It usually takes the subjunctive: «el hecho de que sea caro no importa». The h is silent.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "no digo que",
   "significado": "I'm not saying that",
   "pron": "no DI-go ke",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "A verb of saying in the negative takes the subjunctive: «no digo que sea fácil».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "no significa que",
   "significado": "it doesn't mean that",
   "pron": "no sig-ni-FI-ka ke",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "The subjunctive follows: «no significa que no confíe en ti».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "preocuparse",
   "significado": "to worry",
   "pron": "pre-o-ku-PAR-se",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is pronominal: «me preocupo», «se preocupa». You say «preocuparse por algo».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "confiar en",
   "significado": "to trust",
   "pron": "kon-FYAR en",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "You say «confiar en alguien». In «confío» the accent marks the i.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "abrigo",
   "significado": "coat",
   "pron": "a-BRI-go",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is masculine: «el abrigo». «Abrigarse» is to put on clothes so as not to be cold.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "ponga",
   "significado": "puts on (subjunctive of «poner»)",
   "pron": "PON-ga",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Subjunctive of «poner», to put. Stress on PON: PON-ga.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "insiste",
   "significado": "insists (from «insistir»)",
   "pron": "in-SIS-te",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "From «insistir», to insist. Stress on SIS: in-SIS-te.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "comprendo",
   "significado": "I understand (from «comprender»)",
   "pron": "kom-PREN-do",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "From «comprender», to understand. Stress on PREN: kom-PREN-do.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "preocupe",
   "significado": "worries (subjunctive of «preocuparse»)",
   "pron": "pre-o-KU-pe",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Subjunctive of «preocuparse», to worry. The c before u is k.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "insista",
   "significado": "insists (subjunctive of «insistir»)",
   "pron": "in-SIS-ta",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Subjunctive of «insistir». The s is clear: in-SIS-ta.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "confíe",
   "significado": "trusts (subjunctive of «confiar»)",
   "pron": "kon-FI-e",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Subjunctive of «confiar», to trust. The accent on í breaks the diphthong.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "creas",
   "significado": "you believe (subjunctive of «creer»)",
   "pron": "KRE-as",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Subjunctive of «creer», to believe. The ea is two syllables: KRE-as.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "húmedo",
   "significado": "damp (masculine)",
   "pron": "U-me-do",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "adjective",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "The accent on the first syllable is stressed: U-me-do. The h is silent.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "tiende",
   "significado": "holds out (from «tender»)",
   "pron": "TIEN-de",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "From «tender», to hold out. The ie is a diphthong: TIEN-de.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "mete",
