  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "One verb, two readings",
     "texto": [
      "With **decir, insistir en, recordar, escribir** and **repetir**:\n\n- + indicative, they pass on **information**: insiste en que **es** verdad.\n- + subjunctive, they pass on an **order**: insiste en que **vayamos**.\n\n**Sentir**: siento que **hay** un problema (I sense it); siento que **haya** un problema (I am sorry about it).\n\n**Comprender** and **entender**: comprendo que **estás** cansado (I can see it); comprendo que **estés** cansado (I find it natural).\n\nA verb of saying or thinking in the **negative** takes the subjunctive: **no digo que sea** fácil. **No creo que venga.** A negative command and a question keep the indicative: **no creas que es** fácil; ¿**no crees que es** fácil?\n\n**El hecho de que** usually takes the subjunctive: el hecho de que **sea** caro no importa."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Information or order",
     "texto": [
      "**The mood changes the meaning.**\n\n- decir, insistir en, recordar: + indicative = information; + subjunctive = order.\n- sentir: + indicative = I sense it; + subjunctive = I regret it.\n- comprender: + indicative = I can see it; + subjunctive = I find it natural.\n\n**Negation.** No digo que, no creo que, no significa que → subjunctive. But a negative command and a question keep the indicative: no creas que es fácil."
     ],
     "ejemplos": [
      {
